# Quotes C comment syntax on purpose.
#
# Both delimiters have to survive the trip into a C block comment: a /* opens
# one and a */ closes one, and a doc comment that carries either would
# otherwise warn under -Wcomment or terminate the comment early and spill
# prose into code position. Real definitions do this -- the standard
# namespace and the showroom both quote C and JSDoc syntax when explaining
# what a backend emits.

uint8 value
# Also quotes a /* delimiter, to cover field docs as well as type docs.

@sealed
